dinero-core (8.0.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v8.0.5 stable point release on top of v8.0.4 — shielded wallet fixes.
    - wallet/shielded: the shielded note tree no longer re-appends chain leaves
      on rescan/restart. A confirmed note's leaf_index (and its position-dependent
      nullifier) stays fixed instead of drifting, so shielded spends build valid
      proofs and are accepted across restarts. Wallets corrupted by the prior bug
      self-heal on first open (dedup the tree to canonical order, recompute
      nullifiers). Fixes shielded sends being mempool-rejected after a restart
      (#324).
    - wallet/shielded: an explicit fee below the mempool's size-based floor is now
      rejected up front with a clear error, before the spend is persisted, instead
      of building a tx the mempool rejects (#322).
    - qt/shielded: the "Send shielded" labels show only the active network's
      address prefix (dins on mainnet) instead of listing dins/tdins/rdins (#320).

 -- Dinero Labs <team@dinerolabs.org>  Tue, 23 Jun 2026 18:00:00 -0500

dinero-core (8.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v8.0.4 stable point release on top of v8.0.3.
    - daemon: the RPC server now binds reliably on nodes with a large chaindb /
      many wallets. ChainDB caps RocksDB max_open_files (was unlimited, opening
      all SST files and pushing the process FD count past FD_SETSIZE=1024), and
      the RPC accept loop uses poll() instead of select() (which cannot handle a
      socket fd >= 1024). Fixes the GUI "daemon exited before the wallet could
      connect" failure on long-running nodes (#317).

 -- Dinero Labs <team@dinerolabs.org>  Sun, 21 Jun 2026 15:30:00 -0500

dinero-core (8.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v8.0.3 stable point release on top of v8.0.2. Two consensus fixes
    (both Windows-verified + canary-proven on a live fleet node):
    - consensus(reorg): a miner whose tip block loses the chainwork race no
      longer wedges on its own minority fork; the node now reorgs to the
      higher-work P2P-learned branch (eligibility + body-position metadata),
      with consensus-invalid speculative branches marked failed and the
      pre-reorg tip restored on abort (#310, fixes #309).
    - consensus(asert): getblocktemplate no longer returns too-easy difficulty
      on an AssumeUTXO-snapshot-resynced node; the ASERT anchor-time fallback
      uses block 1's real timestamp instead of genesis, so the template matches
      validation regardless of backfill state (#315, fixes #314).

