 -- Dinero Labs <team@dinerolabs.org>  Mon, 08 Jun 2026 18:10:00 +0000

dinero-core (8.0.0~rc7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * RC7: P2P port-mapping no longer freezes daemon startup.
    - PortMappingSession::Start (miniupnpc SSDP/IGD + libnatpmp probes)
      is now dispatched on a dedicated worker thread by P2PService.
      Previously it ran synchronously on the daemon init thread; on
      routers that responded to SSDP but stalled on SOAP this could
      block the daemon (and dinero-qt's bundled-daemon launch) for
      tens of seconds with no log output. Init now flows through
      Mining/Metrics/RPC immediately; the portmap result lands later
      in NetworkStatus.port_mapping_*.
    - Bounded discovery deadline. New knob
      `p2p.portmap_discovery_timeout=<seconds>` (default 45, minimum
      5) caps how long the worker is allowed to run. should_abort
      probes between each blocking phase (SSDP, IGD lookup, AddPortMapping,
      every NAT-PMP request/response) plus a post-Start backstop drop
      any router mapping that completed after the deadline. Outbound
      P2P is unaffected when the deadline trips.
    - Shutdown is bounded: StopPortMapping signals cancel and joins
      the worker, capped by miniupnpc's own per-syscall timeout.
  * Packaged-service contract unchanged: dinerod + dinero-cli only,
    no Qt, no GPU mining, no gRPC, no hardware-wallet HID. Operators
    who want the GUI install dinero-qt-desktop separately (see the
    v8.0.0-rc7 GitHub release).

