dinero-core (8.0.0~rc6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * RC6 rebuild from a03ecd8c. First release where the daemon actually
    links the UPnP / NAT-PMP runtime on platforms where the libraries
    are available (depends prefix on Windows, system pkg-config on
    Linux). Previous rc4/rc5 cuts shipped --portmap CLI args that
    parsed but always reported the backend unavailable at runtime.
  * Cumulative since rc3 (skipping rc4 which was never tagged in
    public, and rc5 which shipped without UPnP/NAT-PMP runtime):
    - Network-magic refactor: daemon + seeder + every internal call
      site reads the P2P magic from dinero::Params() at runtime;
      seeder header generated from chainparams_impl.cpp. Drift test
      tests/integration/test_network_magic_sync.sh enforces one
      truth path.
    - fuzz/fuzz_p2p_header_standalone.cpp now reads kMagicMainnet
      from the generated seeder header.
    - .gitattributes pins shell-family files to LF, Windows scripts
      to CRLF.
    - Qt UX: prompt before enabling P2P networking, non-blocking
      notice, in-app P2P reachability status.
    - UPnP + NAT-PMP port-mapping deps pinned via depends/ (Bitcoin-
      Core-style ExternalProject pipeline). Native MSVC toolchain
      validated end-to-end on both Ninja and Visual Studio 17 2022
      generators; .pc files now advertise *_STATICLIB defines so any
      pkg-config consumer (not just our CMake) gets the static-lib
      gate. dinerod / dinero-qt now statically link miniupnpc +
      libnatpmp where present.
    - Peer-discovery additions: bridge addrman with p2p relay, peer
      ban controls, advertise NAT-PMP public address.
  * Packaged-service contract unchanged: dinerod + dinero-cli only,
    no Qt, no GPU mining, no gRPC, no hardware-wallet HID. Operators
    who want the GUI install dinero-qt-desktop separately (see the
    v8.0.0-rc6 GitHub release).

